      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>If the yeti jumps at least 20 ft. as part of its movement, it can then use this action to land on its feet in a space that contains one or more other creatures. Each of those creatures must succeed on a DC 18 Strength or Dexterity saving throw (target's choice) or be knocked prone and take 30 (4d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage. On a successful save, the creature takes only half of the damage, isn't knocked prone and is pushed 5 ft. out of the yeti space into an unoccupied space of the creature's choice. If no unoccupied space is within range, the creature instead falls prone in the yeti space.</p>",
